  "live_records": {
    "q-174372": {
      "dom_id": "step-q174372",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Consider the following sets:\n\n$$\nA=\\{5n∣n\\in Z\\},\\,B=\\{-\\frac{1}{n}∣n\\in N\\}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $B=\\{-1,-2,-3,…\\}$\n\nII. $A\\cap B=∅$\n\nIII. $A$ and $B$ are disjoint",
      "worked_solution": "Two sets $A$ and $B$ are *disjoint* if they have no element in common, i.e., their intersection is empty:\n\n$$\nA\\cap B=∅\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets.\n\n- Statement I is false.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =\\{-\\frac{1}{n}∣n\\in N\\} \\\\  & =\\{-1,-\\frac{1}{2},-\\frac{1}{3},…\\} \\\\  & \\ne \\{-1,-2,-3,…\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. Notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\{5n∣n\\in Z\\} \\\\  & =\\{…,-10,-5,0,5,10,…\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, the intersection is \n\n$$\nA\\cap B=\\{…,-10,-5,0,5,10,…\\}\\cap \\{-1,-\\frac{1}{2},-\\frac{1}{3},…\\}=∅.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Since the intersection is empty, the two sets are disjoint.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
