    "q-174426": {
      "dom_id": "step-q174426",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "Find the disjoint union of the sets ${A}_{1}=\\{1,3,5\\}$ and ${A}_{2}=\\{5,10,15\\}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that the sets are overlapping since\n\n$$\n\\{1,3,5\\}\\cap \\{5,10,15\\}=\\{5\\}\\ne ∅.\n$$\n\nSo, for each of our sets, we form the associated set, where each element is tagged with the corresponding index, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {A}_{1} &  & \\,\\to \\, &  & {A}_{1}^{∗}=\\{(1,1),(3,1),(5,1)\\} \\\\  & {A}_{2} &  & \\,\\to \\, &  & {A}_{2}^{∗}=\\{(5,2),(10,2),(15,2)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the disjoint union of our sets is simply the union of the associated tagged sets:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1}⊔{A}_{2} & =\\{1,3,5\\}⊔\\{5,10,15\\} \\\\  & ={A}_{1}^{∗}\\cup {A}_{2}^{∗} \\\\  & =\\{(1,1),(3,1),(5,1)\\}\\cup \\{(5,2),(10,2),(15,2)\\} \\\\  & =\\{(1,1),(3,1),(5,1),(5,2),(10,2),(15,2)\\}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
